    "storage": "Keeps 2 days in the fridge but reheat gently to serve — cold, the coconut fat sets and the texture suffers badly. ⛔ Add the peanuts and sesame fresh each time; stored in the bowl they go soft overnight. The bananas will darken by day two, which looks worse than it tastes.",
    "chefNotes": "Ripe and freckled, not firm and not grey. Cook the tapioca in water you throw away. Never let the coconut milk boil. Salt it more than feels right for a pudding. And keep the nuts off until the bowl is in front of somebody.",
